  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116596",
      "title": "Server-side Rendering (SSR) Introduction",
      "lectureOrder": 319,
      "videoOrder": 302,
      "sourceHash": "cab8fe15652fb67b6ea2c7244a6ba9830da429b290974b098455df7b490c7d53",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.99,
          "en": "So you can build Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.99,
          "end": 6.87,
          "en": "as single page applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.87,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "This has some potential disadvantages, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "which might not matter to you, on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 14.97,
          "en": "but you also have another option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.97,
          "end": 18.54,
          "en": "when it comes to building Angular applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.54,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "You can build a server-side rendered app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 24.57,
          "en": "You can use server-side rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.57,
          "end": 27.603,
          "en": "and that's what SSR stands for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.71,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "Now, that's an Angular app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 33.57,
          "en": "where its routes are actually rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.57,
          "end": 37.86,
          "en": "on-demand on a dynamic web server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 40.95,
          "en": "So instead of just having a single HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.95,
          "end": 44.67,
          "en": "and letting client-side Angular do everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.67,
          "end": 47.4,
          "en": "with a server-side rendered app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.4,
          "end": 51.42,
          "en": "when a user wants to visit a certain page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.42,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "the request is handled on the server first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 59.51,
          "en": "and the page that was requested is pre-rendered on-demand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 60.51,
          "en": "on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.51,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "so that the finished page is sent back to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 66.48,
          "en": "And that's an important difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.48,
          "end": 71.48,
          "en": "Instead of getting that essentially empty, single HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 74.88,
          "en": "and having client-side JavaScript do everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.88,
          "end": 79.773,
          "en": "the user receives the finished page with all its content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.76,
          "end": 82.08,
          "en": "That being said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.08,
          "end": 87.08,
          "en": "that page still includes lots of Angular JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.53999999999999,
          "end": 89.28,
          "en": "which then takes over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.28,
          "end": 93.09,
          "en": "and hydrates the page once it has been received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.09,
          "end": 95.1,
          "en": "by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.1,
          "end": 99.39,
          "en": "So then it will actually become a single page application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.39,
          "end": 102.33,
          "en": "and subsequent actions will be handled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.33,
          "end": 105.03,
          "en": "by client-side JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.03,
          "end": 108.15,
          "en": "so that you get the best of both worlds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.15,
          "end": 112.28999999999999,
          "en": "instant responses due to client-side JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.28999999999999,
          "end": 113.97,
          "en": "doing the heavy work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.97,
          "end": 115.44,
          "en": "but at the same time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.44,
          "end": 118.41,
          "en": "finished pages without missing content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.41,
          "end": 121.11,
          "en": "for the initial request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.11,
          "end": 124.5,
          "en": "Now, when going for a server-side rendered app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.5,
          "end": 127.29,
          "en": "you therefore need a dynamic web server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.29,
          "end": 130.59,
          "en": "which is able to run code on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.59,
          "end": 133.803,
          "en": "as it receives those incoming requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.7,
          "end": 138.06,
          "en": "A server that's just able to return HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.06,
          "end": 142.77,
          "en": "and JavaScript files is no longer enough then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.77,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "Instead, it must be a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 148.82999999999998,
          "en": "that's able to execute Node.js code specifically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.82999999999998,
          "end": 151.89,
          "en": "because it's that compiled JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 155.34,
          "en": "your Angular code compiled to JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.34,
          "end": 159.333,
          "en": "that must be executed on-demand on this server now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 162.48,
          "en": "Now, the advantage of building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.48,
          "end": 165.12,
          "en": "such a server-side rendered app is therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.12,
          "end": 169.98,
          "en": "that users no longer receive an empty HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.98,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "or an almost empty HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "but instead, a file that contains all the content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 179.97,
          "en": "And that's also great for search engine crawlers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.97,
          "end": 184.2,
          "en": "but this approach also has some potential disadvantages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.2,
          "end": 187.98,
          "en": "For example, if rendering a component takes a bit longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.98,
          "end": 191.22,
          "en": "due to some data fetching, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.22,
          "end": 192.9,
          "en": "then it takes a bit longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.9,
          "end": 196.92000000000002,
          "en": "until the user gets back a response to their request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.92000000000002,
          "end": 199.11,
          "en": "So they might be seeing a blank page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.11,
          "end": 202.14,
          "en": "for a couple of milliseconds or seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 204.9,
          "en": "In addition, we have increased complexity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.9,
          "end": 208.35,
          "en": "because we now do need such a dynamic web server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.35,
          "end": 210.69,
          "en": "and we must set up this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.69,
          "end": 212.613,
          "en": "to support server-side rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.51,
          "end": 215.79,
          "en": "But that's exactly what will take a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.79,
          "end": 217.263,
          "en": "in the next lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
